{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","title":"The normal distribution and the 68-95-99.7 rule"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A normal distribution is symmetric and bell-shaped. Its center is the mean, μ; the standard deviation, σ, sets its spread.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The 68–95–99.7 rule"},{"op":"equation","id":"scale","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"z=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}"},{"op":"figure","id":"bell","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4,4],"y":[0,0.45],"axes":"edge","x_label":"z (standard deviations)","y_label":"Probability density"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"density","y":"exp(-x^2/2)/sqrt(2*pi)","domain":[-4,4]},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":0},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.425],"text":"μ","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Area under the curve represents probability. About 68 percent lies within one standard deviation of the mean.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"central","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-1,"to":1},{"kind":"segment","from":[-1,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.15],"text":"68%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule68","anchor":{"el":"scale","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)\\approx68\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Widen the interval to two standard deviations on each side. The enclosed probability rises to about 95 percent.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"wider","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-2,"to":-1},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":1,"to":2},{"kind":"segment","from":[-2,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-2,0.285],"to":[2,0.285],"label":"95%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule95","anchor":{"el":"rule68","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-2\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+2\\sigma)\\approx95\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s4"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bbbb274a-2d01-4ca5-8cfc-b9ebdca3bb3a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Within three standard deviations lies about 99.7 percent, leaving about 0.3 percent outside. This rule applies to normal, not arbitrary, distributions.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"widest","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-3,"to":-2},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":2,"to":3},{"kind":"segment","from":[-3,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-3,0.35],"to":[3,0.35],"label":"99.7%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule997","anchor":{"el":"rule95","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-3\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+3\\sigma)\\approx99.7\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
